# glutarimide.msf
# Glutarimide (2,6-piperidinedione)
# pKa=9.700 (N-H cyclic imide acid, q=0→-1)
# Source: Albert & Serjeant 1971
# Aliphatic cyclic imide N-H, pKa=9.70. Directly interpolates between
# barbituric acid (err=+1.67, pKa=4.01) and saccharin (err=+0.89, pKa=1.60).
# Unlike phthalimide, has no aromatic ring → ΔBO_ring≈0, small ΔBO_XC.
# The contrast phthalimide vs glutarimide teaches the model the effect of
# ring aromaticity on the same cyclic imide N-H motif.

